Package: zuid
Title: Universally Unique Identifiers, Their Encodings and Their Kin
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("yan", role = "cph",
           comment = "Author of the Niceware word list, compiled into src/zuid_tables.c"),
    person("Sqids", role = "cph",
           comment = "Authors of the Sqids blocklist, compiled into src/zuid_tables.c"),
    person("Jetify Inc.", role = "cph",
           comment = "TypeID specification fixtures, tests/testthat/fixtures/typeid/")
  )
Description: Parses, validates, inspects and generates universally unique
    identifiers (UUIDs) of every version defined by RFC 9562
    <doi:10.17487/RFC9562>, and re-encodes them in alternative text forms
    such as Crockford base32, base36, base58, base62, base64url, Proquint
    and Niceware words. The same functions read the fields and creation
    time of related identifier formats: Universally Unique Lexicographically
    Sortable Identifiers (ULID), TypeID, UPID, SCRU128 and SCRU64 (Sortable,
    Clock and Random number-based Unique identifiers), K-Sortable Unique
    Identifiers (KSUID), Snowflake, XID, 'MongoDB' ObjectId, NanoID, Cuid2,
    Sqids and content identifiers (CID). Detection never assumes a format
    that the input does not prove. Identifiers are generated from the
    operating system's entropy source, never from R's random number
    generator. No other package is needed at run time.
